    {
      "id": 221153,
      "name": "jffdougan",
      "username": "jffdougan",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jffdougan/{size}/1882_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-08-23T18:39:42.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"jasonr1023\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/aeb1de/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> jasonr1023:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This would be awesome!&nbsp; I am new to the game - just got the collectors box (kickstarter&nbsp;with all perks) and all of the expansions.We've played through about 10 games.&nbsp; Love it!I am a completionist at heart.&nbsp; I'd love to have these two cards, but is there a way for me to see if I already have them?&nbsp; I'd hate to take them from someone else that needs them for their set.&nbsp;Thanks in advance!!!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The way you'll have them is in the oversized pack: on one side of the Infinitor variant, it will say something like \"Tormented Hero\"; the Kismet variant is something like \"Unsubtle Trickster.\"</p>\n<p>They were originally only released in the (updated) oversized pack; Adam eventually did small art for them to match the other \"normal\" villain character cards. If you've got small character cards matching those descriptions,&nbsp; you've got them.</p>",
